Z||000013||Mark||10-22-2001||10:23 AM||||Many thanks once again to Doug, Sage, Tony, Doug's dad, and the members of the Western PA Fiero Club for hosting and organizing this event.  Interesting place, informative demos, friendly people, beautiful weather, nice cars! What more could you ask for!    <P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Heretic:<BR><B>That gold GT in the third and fourth photos looks hella sweet! nice pics.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The gold GT was recently painted.  Beautiful job.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Reality||10-22-2001||11:26 AM||||The Pearl car is Doug's. Sweet Car I can't remember everything about it, but lets see: Audi Pearl White, 3.4 install by Fiero Factory, T-Top install by Fiero Factory, Mr Mikes leather seats, He upgraded the headlights to the 88 motors, has Blue Xenon projector bulbs, Koni drop spindles, IRM twin dual resonator exhaust, hmm rear sway bar, 16" Prime wheels, well heck just goto;<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/mygarage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/mygarage.html</A><P>The yellow car belonged to a gentleman named Tom I believe he was a local, care to comment on it Doug? Also did anyone take pictures of the inside of the building? That was worth seeing as well. <P><p>[This message has been edited by Reality (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||rogergarrison||10-22-2001||12:03 PM||||The white T-top was beautiful, Im not a big white fan, but with the tan interior it was pretty. The Boxster is real, my friend wanted to go for a cruise since the weather was awesome. She likes all kinds of cars and said to pass along she enjoyed seeing you and all your cars. Its really kind of interesting how close the Boxster is to Fiero in setup and measurements. I didnt take any inside pics because the lighting looked like they wouldnt have come out well. There were a lot of super nice cars inside, not all Fieros. Too bad a lot of people missed out on a great get together on such a nice day. (booooo football fans  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">..)||||reg||1
Z||000016||Sage||10-23-2001||03:37 AM||||Had a good time myself.  Doug runs a pretty tight ship, especially for a one man operation.  Lots of nice cars and great people!  Thumbs up to the PA club for a well executed enjoyable Sunday cruise.  <P>Roger, got some ideas on how to do your car, if you're serious, LMK<P><P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
